f the language options which the app is likely to offer; \n \n(d) whether the Government has  created awareness to popularize this mobile  app \nand if so, the details thereof along with  the total number of districts which are  \ncovered under this system; and \n \n(e) whether any suggestions were  received by the Government for redressal  of \ngrievances and if so, the details thereof  along with the other me asures taken by  \nthe Government to help in real time updation of crime/criminal data? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI G. KISHAN REDDY) \n(a) to (e):      A statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n\n \n--2-- \nStatement referred to in reply to Lok Sabha Starred Question Number 219 \nasked by Shri Sunil Dattatray Tatkare and Shri Kuldeep Rai Sharma  \nregarding web based app on crime for reply on 03.12.2019. \n \n(a) to (e): ‘ Police’ and ‘Public Order’ are State subjects under the Seventh \nSchedule to the Constitution of India. The States are responsible for \nmaintaining law and order, protecting life and property of the citizens in \ntheir respective jurisdictions.  Data on crime and criminals is maintained by \nrespective State s/Union Territories. Information on any web or mobile \nbased application for collection of information related to crime and \ncriminals by the States/UTs is not maintained centrally.  In order to \nfacilitate police in State/ Union Territories with a common plat form for \nfiling reports, collecting and sharing information on crimes and criminals \nat national level,  the Ministry of Home Affairs has implemented the Crime \nand Criminal Tracking Network and Systems . \n***** \n \n  \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|2|STARRED   |22", "t": "Onion  Prices", "head": "LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 22 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON  18th NOVEMBER, 2019 \n \n����������������������������������������\n�\n�������������������������������� �\n�\n���������� ������������������������������������������������