amount of investments made  as a result of the relaxatio n, including the  \nplaces where the investments have been made? \n \nANSWER \nवाणिज  ् य एवं उद्योग मंत्री (श्री पीयूष गोयल)  \nTHE MINISTER OF COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \n(SHRI  PIYUSH GOYAL) \n \n    (a) to (d):    A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n ********  \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION \nNO. 335 FOR ANSWER ON 11.12.2019. \n \n \n(a) & (b):     Government has put in place an investor -friendly policy under which \nFDI up to 100% is permitted under the automatic route in most \nsectors/activities including investments from Non -Resident Indians \n(NRIs). Foreign Direct Investment (FDI) policy is reviewed on an \nongoing basis, with a view to making it more investor friendly, including \nfor NRIs.  \n \nThe extant FDI policy allows special dispensation for NRI investments \nin various sectors such as Construction Development, Civil Aviation \netc. Further, investments made under Schedule IV of FEMA (Non -Debt \nInstruments) Rules, 2019 on non -repatriation basis by NRIs, OCIs and \nCompanies, Trusts and Partnership Firms incorporated outside India \nand owned by such NRIs and OCIs are deemed to be domestic \ninvestment at par with investment made by residents. \n \n(c) & (d): Information in respect of concessions/exemptions given to the NRIs is \nnot centrally maintained. Further, place -wise detail of investment by \nNon-Resident Indians (NRIs) in India is not maintained. However, the \ntotal investment made by NRIs on repatriation basis in Indian \ncompanies along with the total FDI equity inflow reported in the country \nis annexed. \n \n \n \n \n \n********  \n  \n\nANNEXURE \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (c) & (d) OF THE LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 335 FOR ANSWER ON 11.12.2019. \n \nNRI investments -FDI in India —Financial year wise.  \n  \nTable 1: NRI investment through issue of equity instrument in Indian \ncompanies  \nAmount in INR Crores  \nYear wise  FDI inflows (gross)  in India  \n2016-17 1012.34  \n2017-18 1063.14  \n2018-19 1582.15  \n2019-20 (October 2019)  1302.50  \nSource: As reported to RBI by companies in Form FC -GPR declaring the investor type as NRI/OCI \n \n \nTable 2: NRI investment through transfer of equity Instruments (inflows) in \nIndian  companies  \nAmount in INR Crores  \nYear wise  FDI inflows (gross) in India  \n2018-19 (Sept 2018 -March 2019)  38.70  \n19-20 (October 2019)  55.42  \nSource: As reported to RBI by transferor/ transferee/ Indian companies in Form FC-TRS, declaring the \nbuyer type as NRI/OCI \n[Note: Investor- wise (here NRI/OCI) classification is available only from September 01, 2018.]  \n \nTable 3: NRI investment through Portfolio Investment Scheme in equity \ninstruments \nAmount in INR Crores  \nYear wise  Net inflows  \n2016-17 4622.78  \n2017-18 8280.69  \n2018-19 4444.00  \n2019-20 (October 2019)  883.92  \nSource: As reported to RBI by Authorized Dealer Category I Banks in LEG -NRI package  \n \n \n \n******** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|2|STARRED   |336", "t": "Loss of Lives in Avalanches", "head": " \n                                       \n \n \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, COOPERATION AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n336\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n19\nTH\n \nNOVEMBER, \n20\n1\n9\n \n \nFARMER S\nUICIDES OVER LOANS\n \n \n336.     SHRI RAVIKUMAR D:\n \n \nSHRI T.N. PRATHAPAN:\n \n \n \n \nPROF. SAUGATA RAY:\n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n   \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n  \n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a)\n \nwhether  the Government has the data of suicide of farmers in the country, if so, the \ndetails thereof for the last four financial years, State\n-\nwise;\n \n \n(b) \n \nwhether  the Government has any idea about t\nhe loans of farmers who committed \nsuicide, if so, the details of the average liability of a farmer who committed suicide; \n \n \n(c)\n \nwhether the Government has any proposal to write off the existing loans of the farmers \nwho committed suicide as well as those of\n \nsmall and medium farmers, if so, the details thereof; \n \n \n(d)\n \n \nwhether  the Government has the data of waived loans of farmers in the last four \nfinancial years, the details thereof; \n \n \n(e)\n \n \nthe initiatives taken by the Government to support the farmers finan\ncially and increase \ntheir income, the details thereof; and \n \n \n(f)\n \n \nwhether  the Government has any programmes for providing psychological support for \nfarmers to check the instances of suicide among debt ridden farmers, if so, the details thereof?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nM\nINISTER \n \nOF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n    \n(\nSHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR\n)\n \n \na) & (b):\n \nThe National Crime Records Bureau (NCRB) under the Ministry of Home Affairs \ncompiles and disseminates information on suicides in its publication titled ‘Accidental Deaths \nand Suicides \nin India’ (ADSI). These Reports on suicides are available upto 2016 on its website. \n \n \n(c) & (d): \n \nThere is no proposal on waiver of crop loans under consideration of the \nGovernment of India.\n \n \n(e):\n \nAgriculture being a State subject, the State Governments un\ndertake implementation of \nprogrammes/ schemes for the development of the sector. Government of India supplements the \nefforts of the State Governments through various schemes/ programmes. The various schemes/ \nprogrammes of the Government of India are meant \nfor the welfare of farmers by increasing \nproduction and remunerative returns to farmers. A list of various interventions taken by the \nGovernment is at \nAnnexure\n-\nI\n. All these steps of the Government of India are for the welfare of \nthe farmers of the country.\n \nCont.2/\n \n\n \n-\n2\n-\n \n \nThe Government had constituted an Inter\n-\nMinisterial Committee in 2016 to recommend a \nstrategy for Doubling of Farmers’ Income (DFI) by the year 2022. The DFI Committee submitted \nits report and thereafter the Government constituted an Empower\ned Body on 23.01.2019 for \nmonitoring the implementation of the recommendation of the DFI Strategy. \n \n \n(f): \n \nThe Government is supporting implementation of District Mental Health Programme \n(DMHP) under the National Mental Health Programme (NMHP) in 655 distr\nicts of the country for \ndetection, management and treatment of mental disorders/ illness. The DMHP has been \nrestructured to include additional components like suicide prevention services, work place stress \nmanagement, life skills training and counseling in\n \nschools and colleges. Support is also \nprovided for Central/ State Mental Health Authorities, Research and Training and for \ninformation, education and communication (IEC) activities.\n \n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|2|STARRED   |337", "t": "Industrial Development Projects", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \nDEPARTMENT FOR PROMOTION OF INDUSTRY AND INTERNAL TRADE \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 337. \nTO BE ANSWERED ON WEDNESDAY, THE 11TH DECEMBER, 2019. \n \nINDUSTRIAL DEVELOPMENT PROJECTS \n \n*337.  SHRIMATI VANGA GEETHA VISWANATH: \n \nWill the Minister of COMMERCE AND INDUSTRY be pleased to state: \n                      वाणिज्य एवं उद्योग मंत्री \n(a)  whether the Government proposes  to assist the Government of Andhra  \nPradesh for implementation of Backward  Areas Ultra Mega Integrated \nAutomobile Project to develop the most backward and  rural areas in the State \nparticularly the  setting up of automobile industries in  Tirupati, Nellore and \nAnantapur areas and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(b)  whether the Government proposes to develop areas like Satyavedu and Tada \nin Chittoor district of Andhra  Pradesh industrially, given that  Krishnapatnam \nand Chennai ports are near these areas; \n \n(c)  if so, the details thereof and the progress made in this regard; and \n \n(d)  if not, the reasons therefor?  \n \nANSWER \nवाणिज  ् य एवं उद्योग मंत्री (श्री पीयूष गोयल)  \nTHE MINISTER OF COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \n(SHRI  PIYUSH GOYAL) \n \n \n(a) to (d):   A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n       \n***** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK  SABHA STARRED QUESTION \nNO. 337 FOR ANSWER ON 11TH DECEMBER, 2019. \n \n(a):  The Government of Andhra Pradesh, vide G.O. Ms. No. 40 Industries & \nCommerce (P& I) Department dated. 08.03.2017, issued “Ultra Mega \nIntegrated Automobile Projects Policy for Backward Areas of Andhra \nPradesh”.  The policy shall remain in force up to 31 -03-2022. Under \nthis policy, the Government has approved the following fiscal benefit s \ncovering the categories of:  \n \na) Ultra-Mega Integrated Automobile Projects \nb) Associates/ Ancillaries to UMIAP \nc) Land and Infrastucture \nd) Non-fiscal Incentives \ne) Fiscal Incentives and \nf) GST Scenario Fiscal Incentives \n \nThe Government of India has provided investment allowance under \nsection 32AD of the Income Tax Act under “Backward Areas Ultra \nMega Integrated Automobile Projects Policy”.  \n \n(b) & (c): Industrial Corridor Programme is aimed at development of greenfield \nsustainable industrial cities in India which can compete with the best \nmanufacturing and investment destinations in the world creating \nemployment opportunities and economic growth leading to overall \nsocio-economic development. \n \nAfter the Delhi Mumbai Industri al Corridor Project, the Government of \nIndia has planned four more industrial corridors in December, 2016 \nincluding the East Coast Economic Corridor (ECEC) with Vizag \nChennai Industrial Corridor (VCIC) as Phase 1. \n \nThe State of Andhra Pradesh is covered under two Industrial Corridors, \nnamely, Chennai -Bengaluru Industrial Corridor (CBIC) and Vizag \nChennai Industrial Corridor (VCIC).  Priority nodes identified for \ndevelopment are as follows:  \n \ni. Krishnapatnam node under CBIC; \nii. Vishakhapatnam & Chittoor under Phase 1 of VCIC.  \n \nThe Government of Andhra Pradesh has developed an Industrial Park \nat Tada in Nellore District with an extent of 95.15 acres. \n \nA multi product Sri -City Industrial Park has been developed in \nSatyavedu in Chittoor District in an ext ent of 7,000 Acres which \nincludes SEZ and DTA.    \n \n(d):  Question does not arise. \n******* "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|2|STARRED   |338", "t": "Status of Railway Projects", "head": " \n                                       \n \n \n \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, COOPERATION AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n338\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n19\nTH\n \nNOVEMBER, \n20\n1\n9\n \n \n \nSTEPS \nTO AID SUGARCANE FARMERS\n \n \n338. \n \nSHRI KUNWAR DANISH ALI:\n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n   \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n    \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a)\n \n \nthe steps being taken by the Government for the betterment of sugarcane farmers; \n \n \n(b) \n \nwhether it is a fact that a number of sugarcane farmers committed suicide due to their \ninability to repay th\neir bank loan; and \n \n \n(c)\n \n \nif so, the details thereof?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nM\nINISTER \n \nOF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n    \n(\nSHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR\n)\n \n \n(a):\n \nDepartment of Agriculture, Cooperation & Farmers Welfare is implementing Sugarca\nne \ndevelopment programme under National Food Security Mission (NFSM) in 13 major sugarcane  \ngrowing states from 2014\n-\n15 with the aim to increase production and productivity. \n \n \nFurther, t\nhe Central Government fixes the Fair and Remunerative Price (FRP) of \ns\nugarcane before\n \nthe\n \ncommencement of every sugar season. The FRP is a benchmark \nguaranteed price of sugarcane\n,\n \ndetermined by the Government below which no sugar mill can \npurchase sugarcane from cane growers. The Central Government also takes appropriate \nmeasures from time to time to stabilize sugar prices at reasonable level and to improve the \nliquidity position o\nf the mills.     \n \n \n \n(b) & (c):\n \nThe National Crime Records Bureau (NCRB) under the Ministry of Home Affairs \ncompiles and disseminates information on suicides in its publication titled Accidental Death and \nSuicide in India (ADSI).  However, \nspecific informat\nion with\n \nrespect to\n \ns\nuicides by sugarcane \nfarmers is\n \nnot available with the Bureau.\n \n \n*******\n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|2|STARRED   |339", "t": "Construction of FOBs", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.339 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 11.12.2019 \n \nCONSTRUCTION OF FOBs \n \n \n†*339. SHRI SANTOSH PANDEY: \n  \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the number and locations of Foot Over Bridges (FOBs) \nsanctioned for construction under Nagpur, Raipur and Bilaspur \nRailway Divisions during the last three years; \n  \n(b) the number of FOBs completed, under construction and those on \nwhich work has not commenced, the Station wise status thereof;  \nand  \n \n(c) whether FOBs constructed at Rajnandgaon and Dongargarh in \nChhattisgarh have been completed within the stipulated time and if  \nso, the details thereof? \n \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS AND COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \n(SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL) \n \n(a) to (c): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n***** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF STARRED \nQUESTION NO.339 BY SHRI SANTOSH PANDEY TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK \nSABHA ON 11.12.2019 REGARDING CONSTRUCTION OF FOBs 