adhan  Mantri Suraksha Bima Yojana \non payment of a premium of Rs 12/- and Pradhan Mant ri Jeevan Bima Yojana for Rs. \n330/- implemented by the Government mandatory for c rores of Mahatma Gandhi \nNational Rural Employment Guarantee Act (MGNREGA) labourers for their welfare and \nsafety; \n(b) if so, whether there is any proposal to increase the mandays of MGNREGA labourers; \n(c) whether the Government has conducted any assessment  on the aspects of benefits and \nsecurity of the above schemes in respect of MGNREGA labourers; \n(d) if so, the details thereof; and \n(e) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR) \n \n(a)&(b):  No, Sir. \n \n(c):  No, Sir. \n(d):  Does not arise. \n(e):  Welfare measures to workers under Mahatma Gandhi NR EGA at worksite are elaborated \nin Schedule II of Mahatma Gandhi NREGA, 2005. The details are as under: \n \n(i) If any personal injury is caused to any person employed under the Scheme by any \naccident arising out of and in the course of his em ployment, he shall be entitled to \nsuch medical treatment as required, free of cost. \n(ii) Where hospitalisation of the injured worker is  necessary, the State Government shall \narrange for such hospitalisation including accommod ation, treatment, medicines and \npayment of daily allowance which is not less than half of the wage rate. \n(iii) If a person employed under the Scheme meets w ith death or becomes permanently \ndisabled by accident arising out of and in the cour se of employment, he or his legal \nheirs, as the case may be, shall be paid by the implementing agency an ex gratia as per \n\nentitlements under the Aam Aadmi BimaYojana or as m ay be notified by the Central \nGovernment. \n(iv) If any personal injury is caused by accident t o a child accompanying a person who is \nemployed under the Scheme, such person shall be ent itled to medical treatment free of \ncost; and in case of death or disablement of the child due to the said accident, ex gratia \nshall be paid to the legal guardians as determined by the State Government. \n \n******** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|2|UNSTARRED |32", "t": "Case Pendency in NCLTs", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 32  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19.11.2019 \n \nMAHATMA GANDHI NATIONAL RURAL EMPLOYMENT GUARANTEE SCHEME \n \n*32.  SHRI MAGUNTA SREENIVASULU REDDY: \nSHRI CHANDRA SEKHAR BELLANA:  \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT  be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is aware that the averag e entry year in the share of workforce in \nthe age group of 18-30 for the Mahatma Gandhi Natio nal Rural Employment Guarantee \nScheme began moving up after the financial year 2017-18; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether the Government recognizes this as a sig n of rural distress and lack of job \nopportunities for the youth; and \n(d) whether the Government has any plan to alleviat e this lack of job opportunities for the \nyouth in rural areas and if so, the details thereof?  \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR) \n \n \n(a) to (d):  A statement is laid on the Table of the Ho use. \n  \n\nStatement in reply to Parts (a) to (d) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No. 32 for 19.11.2019 \n \n(a)&(b): As per the Management Information System ( MIS), the average share of \nworkforce under \nMahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Scheme (Mahatma \nGandhi NREGS) in the age group of 18-30 during the last four financial years is as under:  \n \nYear \nTotal individuals worked  \n(in lakh) \nTotal individuals worked \nunder the age group \n18-30  (in lakh) \n% of individuals \nworked under age \ngroup 18-30 \n2015-16  722.59 72.74 10.07% \n2016-17  766.91 69.78 9.10% \n2017-18  759.15 58.70 7.73% \n2018-19  777.41 70.74 9.10% \n \n(c): No, Sir. Mahatma Gandhi NREGS  is a demand driven wage employment programme. It \nprovides livelihood security i.e., fall back option  for livelihood for the rural households when no \nbetter employment opportunity is available. The dem and for work is influenced by various \nfactors such as rain-fall, availability of alternat ive and remunerative employment opportunities \noutside Mahatma Gandhi NREGS . An additional 50 days of wage employment is provide d over \nand above 100 days in the notified drought affected  areas or natural calamity areas in the country \non recommendation of the Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare.  \n \n(d): \nDoes not arise. \n \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|2|UNSTARRED |320", "t": "Global Hunger Index", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMtNrsTRy oF coNsuMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & pUBLtc DISTRIBUTTON\nDEPARTMEI{T OF FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED OUESTIOI{ NO. 32O\nTO BE ANSWERED O lgth NOVEMBER,2Ol9\nGLOBAL HUNGER INDEX\n32O. SHRI T.R. BAALU:\nSHRI UTTAM KUMAR REDDY I{ALAMADA:\nSHRI MALOOK NAGAR:\nWill the Minister of GONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD At{D pUBLtC\nDISTRIBUTIOII sffffr err*, urc-a gt{ Ttrfff,r ffi{ur d+ be pteased to\nstate:\n(a) whether lndia is laggang behind even its neighbouring countries like\nPakistan, Eangladesh and l{epal in starvation and malnutrition index and\nif so, the details thereof;\n(b) whether it is a fact that there is overflowing of foodgrain stocks in\nFood Gorporation of lndia (FGI) warehouses and the Ministry of Gonsumer\nAffairs, Food and Public Distribution had said that {{5O metric tonnes of\nfoodgrains are still stored in the godowns in the country and 73,6 million\ntonnes of foodgrains in FGlts central pool are still stored in the godowns\nin the country and if so, the details thereof and the steps taken by the\nGovernment for achieving Sustainable Development Goal of Zero Hunge4\n(c) whether {9 crore people in the country are still sleeping every day\nwithout a morsel for food and if so, the reasons therefo4 and\n(d) whether any measures are being taken to rectifyr the problem of\npersisting hunger/starvation despite overflowing foodgrain stock and\nmake foodgrains more accessible in the country and if so, the details\nthereof?\nANSWER\nIUIINISTER OF STATE FOR MINISTRY OF GONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD &\nPUBLIC DISTRIBUTION\n(sHRr DAilVE RAOSAHEB DADARAO)\n(a): As per information available in the public domain\n(https:/iwww.concern.net/ansa hts/qlobal.hunqer-index-2O{ 9)' ! ndiats\nranking in the Global Hunger Index (GHl) brought out by Concem UUorld\nWide is {O2. Pakistan is ranked 94, Bangladesh is ranked 88 and Nepal is\nranked 73. As per GHI Report 2Ol9 of Concern World Wide, the composite\nGHI scores of lndia have improved from 38.8 in 2OOO to 3O.3 in 2O{9.\nThus, the country has shown consistent improvement over the years.\n....2t-"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|2|UNSTARRED |321", "t": "Culture Fishing and Fishing Assistance", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRYAND DAIRYING  \nDEPARTMENT OF FISHERIES \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.321 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19TH NOVEMBER, 2019 \nCulture Fishing and Fishing Assistance \n321.  SHRI RAM MOHAN NAIDU KINJARAPU: \nWill the Minister of ANIMAL HUSBANDRY, DAIRYING AND FISHERIES मत्स्यपालन, \nपशुपालन और डेयरी मंत्री be pleased to state: \n(a) the steps taken to certify fishermen under Recognition of Prior Learning Scheme; \n(b) the number of trainees enrolled by Agriculture Skill Council of India for the segments of \n‘Culture Fishing’ and ‘Fishing Assistance’ in the country including Andhra Pradesh; \n(c) the placement statistics of such trainees; \n(d) whether such training in the fishery segment also includes the training of disaster \nmanagement; and  \n(e)  if so, the details thereof? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY  AND \nDAIRYING  \n(SHRI PRATAP CHANDRA SARANGI) \n(a):  Recognition of Prior Learning (RPL)  for people engaged in Fishery Sector is being \nundertaken under Pradhan Mantri K aushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY ) and State funded skill \nprogrammes. \n(b):  The total No. of trainees enrolled for RPL by various affiliated Training Providers is as \nunder; \nSegment Enrolled \nCulture Fishing ( Aquaculture Worker, Shrimp \nFarmer and Hatchery Production Worker) 4,445 \nCapture Fishing (Inland capture fisherman cum \nprimary processor, Marine capture fisherman \ncum primary processor) 15,816 \nFishing Assistance RPL  yet to be taken up \nTotal 20,261 \n \n(c):  The trainee enrolled in Recognition of Prior Learning (RPL) Programme are already \nengaged in their respective occupations and no fresh placement is undertaken for them. \n(d) and (e): No Sir.  The Qualification Packs developed cover the skills required for an \nindividual to perform a specific task.  Disaster Management capsule is not included in the \nQualification Packs currently in use. \n**** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|2|UNSTARRED |322", "t": "Schemes for Orphans and Physically Challenged Persons", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF DEFENCE \nDEPARTMENT OF EX-SERVICEMEN WELFARE \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 322 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 11th December, 2019 \n \nWELFARE OF EX-SERVICEMEN \n*322. DR. SHRIKANT EKNATH SHINDE: \nWill the Minister of DEFENCE j{kk ea=h  \nbe pleased to state: \n (a) the details of welfare  and rehabilitation schemes and financial assistance provided \nto ex-servicemen by the Government through various agencies; \n(b) the total amount distributed  for the welfare of ex -servicemen under  Raksha \nMantri’s Discretionary Fund  (RMDF) and the number of beneficiaries  of the Fund \nduring the last three years, year-wise; \n(c) the main activities of Kendriya Sainik Board and the manner in which the activities \nare beneficial to ex-servicemen and their families; and \n(d) the efforts made to activate Grievances Redressal Mechanism for ex-servicemen \nand to expedite the redressal of their grievances? \n \n \nA    N    S    W    E    R \n \nMINISTER OF DEFENCE                                    (SHRI RAJNATH SINGH) \n      j{kk ea=h                  ¼Jh राजनाथ  स िंह  ) \n \n \n(a) to (d):  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n******* \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 322 FOR ANSWER ON 11.12.2019 \nREGARDING ‘WELFARE OF EX-SERVICEMEN’.  \n(a) The Welfare, Rehabilitation Scheme and Financial Assistance is provided by the \nGovernment through  Kendriya Sainik Board  (KSB), Directorate General Resettlement  \n(DGR) and the Service Headquarters. In addition various State Governments also have \nseparate schemes for welfare of Ex-servicemen (ESM).     \nDetails of Schemes run by KSB are at Annexure- A \n \nDetails of Rehabilitation schemes run by DGR are at Annexure –B \n \nDetails of measures instituted by Service Headquarters are at Annexure- C \n \n(b)  The nomenclature of Raksha Mantri’s Discretionary Fund (RMDF) has been \nchanged to Raksha Mantri’s Ex -Servicemen Welfare Fund (RMEWF). The details of \ntotal amount distributed along with number of beneficiaries for the welfare of Ex -\nservicemen under Raksha Mantri Ex-Servicemen Welfare Fund (RMEWF) during last  \nthree years  is as under :- \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n (c) Details of the main activities of Kendriya Sainik Board are  placed at Annexure- D \n \n All the above activities are primarily for the welfare of Ex -servicemen and their \ndependents  to  lead a dignified life after retirement. It may be seen that the support \ncreated through the various schemes like penury grant, daughters’ marriage grant, \neducation grant, disabled children grant, house repair grant, medical treatment grant , \nserious disease grant, orphan grant etc have resulted in more compassionate support to \nthe families and children of ex -servicemen.  The educational opportunities of ex -\nservicemen’s children have been expanded.  A growing involvement of civil society and \nthe private sec tor with ex -servicemen’s welfare has resulted in improved mobilization \nof welfare funds. \n \n \n...2/- \nFinancial \nYear \nNo of \nbeneficiaries \nTotal Amount \nDisbursed \nRs (In Crores) \n2016-17 37,572 67.21 \n \n2017-18 29,303 57.81 \n \n2018-19 \n \n24,066 64.40 \n \nTotal  90,941 189.42 \n\n: 2 : \n \n A total of 90941 ESMs and their dependents have been benefited under these \nschemes during last three years (from 2016-17 to 2018-19). \n \n \n(d) Redressal o f  grievances is a key function of the Department of Ex -Servicemen \nWelfare. In the direction of prompt and satisfactory resolution of grievances, the \nfollowing initiatives were taken subsequent to 2014 :-  \n \n(i) Personal contact with petitioners  : Apart from written communications, \npetitioners are contacted over phone to obtain specifics of the grievance \nincluding service/pensioners’ details, Feedback about resolution of grievances  \nand  to ascertain level of satisfaction.  \n(ii) Categorization of grievances: The department has categorized the grievances \nin 27 categories according to the nature of grievances received from ex -\nservicemen to know the cause of the grievances and issuing instructions to the \nconcerned offices for redressal. \n(iii) Periodical monitoring at higher level: The status of pending pension \ngrievances is being monitored at the highest level of the department by the \nSecretary in regular weekly meetings. \n(iv) Synergy of the existing infrastructure: The existing set up of Sainik Boards \nis being u tilized for assisting the petitioners and other ex -servicemen for \ncompletion of documents/Records required for release of pension and assisting \nin State Govt. related issues/grievances. \nOverall percentage of disposal of grievances is 97% and the data are a vailable \nin the pgportal.gov.in. This has been achieved due to intense follow up, regular \ninteraction with the concerned offices as well as weekly review.  The impact of the \nabove indicated initiatives, together with strict compliance with shorter timeline of \n30 days for resolution of grievances and use of technology has resulte"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|2|UNSTARRED |323", "t": "Disinvestment of PSUs", "head": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 323 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 11.12.2019 \n \nRAILWAY PROJECTS  \n \n†*323. SHRI BHAGIRATH CHOUDHARY:  \n \n   Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state:   \n \n(a) the details of new railway projects sanctioned in the State of Rajasthan \nduring the last five years, zone-wise and year-wise; \n  \n(b) the number of projects sanctioned during the last five years on which \nwork is going on at present along with project -wise details of expenditure \nincurred so far; \n \n(c) whether the Government proposes to sanction any new project in the \nState; and  \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n \n \n \nANSWER  \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS AND COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \n(SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL) \n \n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n \n***** \n  \n\n \n \n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 323 BY SHRI BHAGIRATH CHOUD HARY TO BE ANSWERED IN \nLOK SABHA ON 11.12.2019 REGARDING RAILWAY PROJECTS \n \n(a) and (b): Railway projects are not sanctioned State -wise, but Zone -wise, \nwhose jurisdiction cuts across the State boundaries. However, during the last \nfive years and current year (2014 -15 to 2018-19 and 2019-20), 04 new lines, 01 \ngauge conversion and 08 dou bling projects covering a total length of 1,772 km \nand costing `23,206 crore falling fully/partly in the State of Rajasthan were \nincluded in Railway Budget. The details of these projects are appended. \n \nDuring 2009 -14, 798 Km length (61 Km New Line, 675 Km Gauge \nConversion and 62 Km Doubling ) has been commissioned in the S tate of \nRajasthan at an average rate of 160 Km per year. \n \nDuring 2014 -19, 1516 Km (80 Km New Line, 483 Km Gauge Conversion \nand 953 Km Doubling) has been commissioned in the State of Rajasth an at an \naverage rate of 303 Km per year, which is 190% of commissioning during   \n2009-14. \n \nAverage Annual Budget allocati on for infrastructure projects and  safety \nworks, falling fully/partly in the State of Rajasthan, during 2014 -19 has been \nenhanced to `2951 crore per year,  from `682 crore per year (during 2009 -14). \nThus, the average annual budget allocation during 2014 -19 is 433% of average \nannual budget allocation of 2009-14 (`682 crore per year). \n \n(c) and (d): Sanction of projects for development of Railways is a continuous \nprocess. Railway projects are sanctioned, based on demands raised by State \nGovernments, Central Ministries, Members of Parliament, other public \nrepresentatives and Railways’ own requirement, participation by State \nGovernment or pri vate entities etc. They are taken up on the basis of \nremunerativeness, last mile connectivity, missing links and alternate routes \netc. \n*****  \n\n \n \nAPPENDIX REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) AND (b) OF STARRED QUESTION \nNO. 323 BY SHRI BHAGIRATH CHOUDHARY TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON \n11.12.2019 REGARDING RAILWAY PROJECTS \nS. \nNo. \nName of \nProject \nYear of \ninclusion\n/ \nsanction \nin \nBudget \nZonal \nRailway \nLatest \nanticipated \ncost \n(` in crore) \nExp-\nenditure \nupto \nMarch \n2019 (` \nin crore) \nOutlay \nfor 2019-\n20 (` in \ncrore) \nStatus \nDoubling \n1. Nimach-\nChittaur\ngarh \n(55.73 \nKm) \n2015-16 Western \nRailway \n389.99 165.33 139 Shambhupura-\nChittaurgarh \n(13.10 km): \nCommissioned. \nWorks taken up \nin balance \nsection. \n2. Phulera- \nDegana \n(108 Km) \n2015-16 North \nWestern \nRailway \n686 4.43 150 Land \nacquisition \ntaken up. (14.70 \nHa  out of 27 Ha \nland has been \nacquired). \nWork taken up \nin available \nland. \n3. Mathura-\nJhansi \n3rd line \n(274 Km) \n2015-16 North \nCentral \nRailway \n3677.76 343 276 Land \nacquisition, \nforest/wild life \nclearance have \nbeen taken up. \nThere is an \nissue of forestry \nclearance in Taj \nTrapezium \nZone. Final \ndecision is \npending with \nHon’ble \nSupreme Court. \nWork taken up \nin available \nland. \n4. Degana-\nRai Ka \nBagh \n(145 Km) \n2018-19 North \nWestern \nRailway \n808.85 12.40 76 Work taken up \nin available \nland. \n  \n\n \n \n \nS. \nNo. \nName of \nProject \nYear of \ninclusion\n/ \nsanction \nin \nBudget \nZonal \nRailway \nLatest \nanticipated \ncost \n(` in crore) \nExp-\nenditure \nupto \nMarch \n2019 (` \nin crore) \nOutlay \nfor 2019-\n20 (` in \ncrore) \nStatus \n5. Agra \nFort-\nBandi \nkui ( 150 \nKm) \n2018-19 North \nCentral \nRailway \n1519.12 Expenditure is not incurred as  the \nProject has been included in Budget \n2018-19 subject to requisite \nGovernment clearances. However, an \noutlay of `0.10 crore has been \nprovided for this project for the year \n2019-20. \n6. Mathura-\nDholpur \n4th line \n(107 Km) \n2018-19 North \nCentral \nRailway \n2945.75 Expenditure is not incurred as  the \nProject has been included in Budget \n2018-19 subject to requisite \nGovernment clearances. However, an \noutlay of `0.10 crore has been \nprovided for this project for the year \n2019-20. \n7. Dhaulpur\n-Jhansi-\nBina 4th \nline  \n(321.80 \nKm) \n2018-19 North \nCentral \nRailway, \nWest \nCentral \nRailway \n4869.95 Expenditure is not incurred as  the \nProject has been included in the \nBudget 2"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|2|UNSTARRED |324", "t": "Strengthening of Panchayati Raj System", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA MINISTRY OF COMMERCE & INDUSTRY (DEPARTMENT OF COMMERCE) LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 324 TO BE ANSWERED ON 11 th DECEMBER, 2019 TO BE ANSWERED ON 11 th DECEMBER, 2019 \nINDIA’S SHARE IN GLOBAL TRADE *324. SHRI SYED IMTIAZ JALEEL: SHRI ASADUDDIN OWAISI: Will the Minister of COMMERCE & INDUSTRY (वािण�य एवं उ�ोग मं�ी ) be pleased to state: pleased to state: (a) whether a high -level advisory group constituted to look at ways to increase India’s share in global trade has submitted its report to the Government; (b) if so, the detailed recommendations made in the report; (c) whether the group has suggested taking steps towards reforming labour laws, tax system, easing entry rules and doing away with protectionist policies; (d) if so, the follow up action taken/ being taken by the Government on the recommendations of the group to increase the share of trade; and (e) the other steps taken/being taken by the Government for reforms in different sectors following the corporate tax reforms? \nANSWER okf.kT; ,oa m|ksx ea=h ( Jh ih;w’k xks;y )THE MINISTER OF  COMMERCE AND INDUSTRY (SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL) (SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL) \n(a) to (e):  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. *****\n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) to (e) OF LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 324   FOR ANSWER ON 11 th DECEMBER,2019 REGARDING “INDIA’S SHARE IN GLOBAL TRADE ”.(a) Yes, Sir. (b) and (c) : Detailed recommendations of the HLAG are available on the website of the Department of Commerce ( https://commerce.gov.in ). (d) The suggesti ons and recommendations of the report of the HLAG have been shared with the   different departments concerned .(e) As regards reforms in tax system, it is stated that through Taxation Laws (Amendment) Ordinance, 2019 (the Ordinance), corporate tax rates have been reduced to 22% plus applicable surcharge and cess for all domestic corporate persons not claiming any deduction or incentive.  Further, an option has been given to any new domestic deduction or incentive.  Further, an option has been given to any new domestic manufacturing companies incorporated on or after 01.10.2019 to avail lower corpora te tax rates of 15% with applicable surcharge and cess without claiming any deduction or incentive as per sub -section (2) of the section 115BAB of the Act, provided they commence manufacturing or production of an article or thing by 31.03.2023. Government has already carried out a number of reforms in various sectors and the reform process is a continuous process for the improvement in the economy. Some of these are by way of amendments in various acts such as the Finance (amendment) Bills, The Special Economic Zones (Amendment) Bill, Amendments in the Goods and Services Tax Act, the Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code ,etc.   ***** ***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|2|UNSTARRED |325", "t": "Compensation for Natural Calamities", "head": "Contd…2/\n-\n \n \n-\n \n2 \n-\n \n \nInterest Subvention Scheme (ISS) was launched in the year 2006\n-\n07 with a view to \nprovide concessional s\nhort term crop loans including loan availed through Kisan Credit Card \n(KCC) to the farmers. Interest subvention of 2% and prompt repayment incentive of 3% on \nrestructured crop loans is given to farmers affected by severe natural calamities. \n \n \n(c)\n:\n \nThe Government is already providing urea to farmers at subsidized rates. Urea is \nbeing provided to the farmers at a statutorily notified Maximum Retail Price (MRP). The MRP \nof 45 kg bag of urea is Rs.242 per bag (exclusive of charges towards neem coating a\nnd \ntaxes as applicable) and the MRP of 50 kg bag of urea is Rs.268 per bag (exclusive of \ncharges towards neem coating and taxes as applicable). The difference between the \ndelivered cost of urea at farm gate and net market realization by the urea units is g\niven as \nsubsidy to the urea manufacturer/importer by the Government of India. The Government of \nIndia is also granting subsidy on P&K fertilizers under the Nutrient Based Subsidy scheme. \nUnder the policy, the subsidy on P&K fertilizers is announced by the \nGovernment on an \nannual basis before the beginning of each financial year. The Subsidy is announced for each \nnutrient i.e Nitrogen (N), Phosphorus (P), Potash (K) and Sulphur (S) on per kg basis, which \nis converted into subsidy per tonne depending upon the\n \nnutrient content in each grade of \nthese fertilizers. MRP (Maximum Retail Price) of P&K fertilizers has been allowed to be fixed \nby manufactures/ importers at reasonable level. Presently, NBS Policy is applicable on 21 \nGrades of P&K fertilizers.\n \n******\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|2|UNSTARRED |326", "t": "Subsidy to Fertilizer Plants", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF MINES \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 326 \nANSWERED ON 11.12.2019 \n \nFUTURE OF MINING \n \n \n*326. SHRI BHAGWANTH KHUBA: \n \nWill the Minister of MINES be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the future of mining in our country appears uncertain due to the legal \nframework, resource overuse, environmental concerns, etc.; and  \n(b)   if so, the details thereof and the manner in which the Government plans to address \nthe above and other related issues?  \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF MINES, COAL AND PARLIAMENTARY AFFAIRS  \n(SHRI PRALHAD JOSHI) \n \n \n(a) to (b): A statement is laid on the table of the House. \n \n \n  \n\nTHE STATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 326 REGARDING “FUTURE OF MINING” RAISED BY SHRI \nBHAGWANTH KHUBA, FOR REPLY ON 11.12.2019. \n \n(a) and (b):- No, Sir. The Central Government has taken various steps for development \nof mining sector in the country. The Mines and Mineral (Development and Regulation) \n(MMDR) Act, 1957 was amended w.e.f. 12.01.2015 and auction has been introduced as \na method of allocation of mining leases to bring greater transparency in the mining \nsector. The Cent ral Government has made certain other amendments and works \ntogether with the State Governments for effective implementation of the Act and the \nRules.  \n \nThe Central Government has also formulated National Mineral Policy, 2019 for a \nvibrant and forward looking mineral sector.  \n \nConsidering the future of mining industry National Mineral Exploration Trust has \nbeen constituted under Section 9(C) of the MMDR Act for taking up detailed and \nregional exploration and studies for mineral development. Geological Survey  of India \n(GSI) and Mineral Exploration Corporation Limited (MECL) have  been entrusted the \nwork of exploration in mining sector. Various Central and State Government agencies \nhave been notified under section 4 of MMDR Act for undertaking exploration.  \n \nThe Central Government has also amended the Mineral Conservation and \nDevelopment Rules, 2017 and the concept of star rating and the period to achieve the \nstar rating have been modified considering the problem s faced by the medium and \nsmall mine owners.  \n \n \n***** \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|2|UNSTARRED |327", "t": "Compensation Scheme for Crop Loss due to Extreme Rain", "head": "������������������� �\n�������������������� �\n�\n��������� �\n������������������������ �\n���������������������������� �\n�\n�������������������������������������������� �\n�\n����������������������������� ��\n�\n� �������������������������������������������������� �\n�\n�� �� ��������������� �������������������������������������� �������\n��������� ��������� �������� ���� �������� ������������ ������\n��������������������������� �\n�\n�� �� �������� ������ ��� ���� �������� ����� ������ ��������� ����\n�����������������������������������������������������������\n���������� �\n�\n�� �� ���������������������������������������������������������������\n���� ������ ��� ������ ����� ���� ������� ���� ������� ���������\n��������������������������� ��\n�\n�\n�\n������ �\n�\n�������������������������������������������� �\n�\n������������������� �\n�\n�\n�� �� ������������������������������������������������������� �\n�\n����� �\n\n�\n���������� ��������� ��� ��� ������ ��� ������ ���� ��� ���� ���\n�������������������������������������������������������\n��� ��������� ��� ���� ������ ��� ����������� ����������\n������������������������������������ �������� �\n�\n�\n������������ ���� ����� ����� ������ ����� ���� ���� ��� ���� ���� ������\n������������� �� ������ ������� ��� ������ ������